From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:33:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable the GPU for the G16
 identity report

NOT FOR MERGE: for one gated identification boot only.

With the GPU node enabled, a kernel with CONFIG_DRM_ASAHI_G16 probes the
J604 GPU once the asahi module is loaded, logs the loaded firmware
identity and the original ADT performance states, and fails the probe
with -ENODEV before the PMP, the driver's own power-domain hold or any
firmware-visible write. The driver core still powers ps_gfx on for the
probe and off again when the probe fails. m1n1 publishes the GPU
reservations it validates and leaves the node as it is, or disables it
again and logs that the handoff is unqualified.

Only the gpu node changes. agx_mbox, gfx_tvm, the PMP and the six
reserved-memory nodes keep their state, and ps_gfx keeps its parent.
PCIe port 0, the USB-C ports and the AOP group stay disabled as on tier
e-lite. The file header no longer claims that the GPU stays disabled.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
index ea5a870c40..b6d97e04fa 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
@@ -9,9 +9,10 @@
  * publishes the firmware segment layout on the gpu node; it never enables
  * the gpu node itself.
  *
- * The GPU, its mailbox and the GFX TVM gate stay disabled: the G16 backend
- * is qualified on J713 only, and the J604 perf-state selection and loaded
+ * The mailbox and the GFX TVM gate stay disabled: the G16 backend is
+ * qualified on J713 only, and the J604 perf-state selection and loaded
  * firmware image are not measured yet. ps_gfx keeps its current parent.
+ * The gpu node itself is enabled only for the identity report below.
  *
  * DTV-<id> tags name rows of DT-VERIFY-gpu.tsv.
  *
@@ -84,7 +85,15 @@
 				<&gpu_shared_l2>, <&gpu_fw_text>, <&gpu_fw_data>;
 		memory-region-names = "ttbs", "pagetables", "handoff",
 				      "shared-l2", "fw-text", "fw-data";
-		status = "disabled"; /* DTV-GPU-7 */
+		/*
+		 * Enabled for the G16 identity report only: the backend refuses
+		 * the J604 before the PMP, its own power-domain hold or the
+		 * firmware (the driver core still powers ps_gfx for the probe
+		 * and off again when it fails), and m1n1 disables this node
+		 * again if the handoff does not match. The mailbox, gfx_tvm and
+		 * the reservations stay as they are.
+		 */
+		status = "okay"; /* DTV-GPU-7 */
 	};
 
 	agx_mbox: mailbox@302608000 {
